* {{a|US}} {{enPR|dŭn}}, {{IPA|en|/dʌn/}}
* {{audio|en|En-ca-done.ogg|Audio (CA)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌn|s=1}}
* {{homophone|en|dun|Donn|Donne|Dunn|Dunne}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# Having [[complete|completed]] or [[finish|finished]] an activity.
#: {{ux|en|He pushed his empty plate away, sighed and pronounced "I am '''done'''."}}
#: {{ux|en|They were '''done''' playing and were picking up the toys when he arrived.}}
# {{lb|en|of an activity or task}} Completed or finished.
#: {{ux|en|I'll text you when the movie's '''done'''.}}
# {{lb|en|of food}} [[ready|Ready]], fully [[cooked]].
#: {{ux|en|As soon as the potatoes are '''done''' we can sit down and eat.}}
# Being [[exhausted]] or fully [[spent]].
#: {{ux|en|When the water is '''done''' we will only be able to go on for a few days.}}
# Without [[hope]] or [[prospect]] of [[completion]] or [[success]].
#: {{ux|en|He is '''done''', after three falls there is no chance he will be able to finish.}}
# [[fashionable|Fashionable]], [[socially]] acceptable, [[tasteful]].
#: {{ux|en|I can't believe he just walked up and spoke to her like that, those kind of things just aren't '''done'''!}}
#: {{ux|en|What is the '''done''' thing these days? I can't keep up!}}

